      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering External Tools**\n\nI'm focusing on external providers for invoice data extraction, and right now Google Cloud's Document AI seems like a viable path to explore further. I need to make sure the code clearly indicates the use of this external service.\n\n\n**Defining the Extraction Function**\n\nNow, I'm defining the `extract_invoice_fields` function within `extract_invoice_fields.py`. It takes a file path as input, which assumes the invoice is a local file. The function's core will involve initializing the Google Cloud Document AI client and then processing the invoice to extract vendor, date, total, and line items. The structure is taking shape.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865778000,
          "start": 1789865774569
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc504de9001rbTvtfholeOi5W",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc504867001TphR5ilHtRq0sd",
      "session_id": "ses_f43afb813ffejULnoTtU6pvZRV",
      "time_created": 1789865774569,
      "time_updated": 1789865778001
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "nKVNkO1PyPJnV3Om",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom google.api_core.client_options import ClientOptions\nfrom google.cloud import documentai_v1 as documentai\n\ndef extract_invoice_fields(project_id: str, location: str, processor_id: str, file_path: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts vendor, date, total, and line-item fields from an invoice using Google Cloud Document AI.\n    \"\"\"\n    # You might need to set up authentication (e.g., GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS)\n    # For more details, see: https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/production\n\n    opts = ClientOptions(api_endpoint=f\"{location}-documentai.googleapis.com\")\n    client = documentai.DocumentProcessorServiceClient(client_options=opts)\n\n    name = client.processor_path(project_id, location, processor_id)\n\n    with open(file_path, \"rb\") as image:\n        image_content = image.read()\n\n    raw_document = documentai.RawDocument(\n        content=image_content,\n        mime_type=\"application/pdf\"  # Assuming PDF invoices; adjust if needed\n    )\n\n    request = documentai.ProcessRequest(name=name, raw_document=raw_document)\n    result = client.process_document(request)\n    document = result.document\n\n    extracted_data = {\n        \"vendor_name\": None,\n        \"invoice_date\": None,\n        \"total_amount\": None,\n        \"line_items\": []\n    }\n\n    for entity in document.entities:\n        if entity.type == \"supplier_name\":\n            extracted_data[\"vendor_name\"] = entity.mention_text\n        elif entity.type == \"invoice_date\":\n            extracted_data[\"invoice_date\"] = entity.mention_text\n        elif entity.type == \"total_amount\":\n            extracted_data[\"total_amount\"] = entity.mention_text\n        elif entity.type == \"line_item\":\n            line_item_data = {}\n            for prop in entity.properties:\n                if prop.type == \"description\":\n                    line_item_data[\"description\"] = prop.mention_text\n                elif prop.type == \"amount\":\n                    line_item_data[\"amount\"] = prop.mention_text\n                # Add other line item properties as needed (e.g., quantity, unit_price)\n            if line_item_data:\n                extracted_data[\"line_items\"].append(line_item_data)\n\n    return extracted_data\n\n",
            "filePath": "extract_invoice_fields.py"
          },
